From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wasm64 port <wasm64@localhost>
Date: Thu, 08 Oct 2026 16:05:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wasm64 port: Mathlib v4.34.0 module names and push_neg
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Game/Metadata.lean: `import Mathlib.Data.Set.Lattice` -> the five modules
  it re-exports (`Mathlib.Data.Set.Lattice.{Bounded,Disjoint,Image,Indexed,
  Order}`). Mathlib v4.34.0 keeps the old name only as a deprecated_module
  shim, which warns when Game/Metadata.lean is compiled (the module that
  imports it; levels importing the metadata do not repeat it); the
  environment is unchanged.
- Game/CustomTactic/PushNeg.lean (new, imported from Metadata): the macro
  Mathlib's own deprecation message recommends, so the taught `push_neg`
  (= `push Not` in Mathlib v4.34.0) no longer logs "`push_neg` has been
  deprecated. Prefer using `push Not` instead." — a warning that made every
  level solved with it (Complement 4 teaches it; Combo 1, FamCombo 1, 2, 5
  and 7 use it) finish "with warnings" instead of completing. Behaviour is
  identical; the inventory's locked-tactic check is atom-based and still
  sees `push_neg`.

No level or world removed; nothing a player types changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Game/CustomTactic/PushNeg.lean | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 Game/Metadata.lean             |  8 +++++++-
 2 files changed, 24 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 Game/CustomTactic/PushNeg.lean

diff --git a/Game/CustomTactic/PushNeg.lean b/Game/CustomTactic/PushNeg.lean
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0470e8c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Game/CustomTactic/PushNeg.lean
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+import Mathlib.Tactic.Push
+
+/-!
+# `push_neg` without the deprecation warning (wasm64 port)
+
+Mathlib v4.34.0 implements `push_neg` as `push Not`, and its `push_neg` elaborator
+unconditionally logs "`push_neg` has been deprecated. Prefer using `push Not` instead." — a
+warning a player would see in every level that uses `push_neg` (taught in Complement level 4),
+which makes the level finish "with warnings" instead of completing it. Mathlib's own deprecation
+text recommends exactly this macro for projects that keep `push_neg`; `priority := high` makes
+it win over Mathlib's parser so no choice node (and no warning) is produced. Behaviour is
+identical: `push_neg`, `push_neg at h`, `push_neg at *`, `push_neg +distrib`.
+-/
+
+open Lean.Parser.Tactic in
+macro (priority := high) "push_neg" cfg:optConfig loc:(location)? : tactic =>
+  `(tactic| push $cfg:optConfig Not $[$loc]?)
diff --git a/Game/Metadata.lean b/Game/Metadata.lean
index 82dd74f..6385d2f 100644
--- a/Game/Metadata.lean
+++ b/Game/Metadata.lean
@@ -2,7 +2,13 @@ import GameServer
 import Mathlib.Tactic.Common
 import Mathlib.Tactic.Have
 import Mathlib.Data.Set.Basic
-import Mathlib.Data.Set.Lattice
+import Game.CustomTactic.PushNeg -- wasm64 port: `push_neg` as `push Not`, without Mathlib's deprecation warning
+-- wasm64 port: Mathlib v4.34.0 keeps Mathlib.Data.Set.Lattice only as a deprecated shim for these five modules
+import Mathlib.Data.Set.Lattice.Bounded
+import Mathlib.Data.Set.Lattice.Disjoint
+import Mathlib.Data.Set.Lattice.Image
+import Mathlib.Data.Set.Lattice.Indexed
+import Mathlib.Data.Set.Lattice.Order
 
 attribute [default_instance] Set.instSingletonSet
 
